# afwdev (Python)

## Layout
- Entry shim: `src/afw_dev/afwdev.py` (zipapp `afwdev:main`; also `./afwdev` from package root). Re-exports `main` and `afwdev_info`.
- CLI: `_afwdev/cli/` — `info.py` (`_info_*` metadata), `parser.py`, `registry.py` (explicit `SUBCOMMAND_HANDLERS`), `settings.py`, `handlers/`.
- Scaffold: `_afwdev/scaffold/` — shared make-*/add-* helpers and handlers.
- Other: `_afwdev/{generate,build,test,validate,common}/`.
- Options keys: see `_afwdev/cli/options.py`. Prefer snake_case `optionName` in `_info_*`; register new subcommands in both `info.py` and `registry.py`.

## Generate pipeline
- Orchestration: `_afwdev/generate/generate.py` — wipes `src/<srcdir>/generated/` then runs bindings, interfaces, strings, cmake fragments, etc.
- Generators must write only under `generated/` (or documented outputs). Never instruct agents to patch generated C/headers by hand.
- Deeper generator guidance: `.cursor/rules/afw-afwdev-generate.mdc` (applies when editing `_afwdev/generate/`).

## Conventions
- Follow surrounding Python style in `_afwdev` (existing modules are the style guide).
- Use `afw-package.json` / `package` helpers in `_afwdev.common` for srcdir discovery; respect `--srcdir-pattern`.
- Prefer extending an existing generator module over duplicating logic.
- Optional per-srcdir hook: `generate/additional_generate/additional_generate.py`.
- Doxygen (`@file` / `@brief` / `@details` / …) is used for afwdev docs. Keep it; do not add changelog or attribution comments.

## Handbook XML (`build --docs` / `--fulldev`)

- Source: `src/*/doc/**/*.xml`. Renderer: `_afwdev/build/docs/docs.py` + `docs_html.py`.
- Supported inline tags include **`literal`** (→ `<code>`), **`strong`**, **`italic`**. Tags must have both a branch in `docs.py` **and** a method on `DocsHtml` (templates under `_resources/html_templates/`).
- Unsupported tags log **`Unknown element: …`** (e.g. DocBook **`emphasis`** is not recognized). Missing methods crash the docs build (`AttributeError`).
- **`--cdev` does not build the handbook.** Prefer **`./afwdev build --fulldev`** before commit/push when docs (or broader work) changed (`--all --generate --clean --install --scan` + `-j`). Docs-only exists; `--fulldev` is not much longer and also regenerates version headers / scans C.

## Related commands agents run
```bash
# Use ./afwdev when the build installs/refreshes afwdev itself
./afwdev build --cdev          # implies -j
afwdev test -j
afwdev validate --pattern '...'
./afwdev build --fulldev       # full package dev install (C, docs, JS, scan); implies -j
```
